{{also|dispensé}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|despenser|lang=fro}} (Modern French {{term|dépenser|lang=fr}}) < {{etyl|la}} {{term|lang=la|dispensare||to weight out, pay out, distribute, regulate, manage, control, dispense}}, frequentative of {{term|lang=la|dispendere||to weight out}} < {{term|lang=la|dis-||apart}} + {{term|lang=la|pendere||to weigh}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-dispense.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛns}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|dispenses|dispensing|dispensed|dispensed}}

# To [[issue]], [[distribute]], or put out.
#*'''1955''', William Golding, ''The Inheritors'', Faber and Faber 2005, p. 40:
#*:The smoky spray seemed to trap whatever light there was and to '''dispense''' it subtly.
# To [[eliminate]] or do without–used intransitively with ''with''.
#: ''I wish he would '''dispense''' with the pleasantries and get to the point.''

